# Generated artefacts are produced with LF endings (scripts/build_frozen_report.py and
# scripts/build_fixture.py both write with newline="\n" or newline=""), and the parity test
# (tests/test_report_matches_fixture.py) checks the committed report byte for byte against a
# fresh render. Without this file, core.autocrlf=true rewrites these files with CRLF on
# checkout on Windows, so every Windows clone starts with a spurious "modified" file before
# the reader has touched anything.
*.html text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
